WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:02.380
"Damn. Stop it."

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.000
"I'm unbreakable. Unbreakable."

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:11.580
Patches: The Hyena. The spider. The Trustworthy. The Unbreakable.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:17.980
The fact he makes it to the end of the world, never truly hollowing, is nothing short of incredible.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:23.360
For we've come across countless undead who lost their humanity in pursuit of a purpose

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.920
yet long after they're gone, Patches remains.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.660
Any undead who makes it to the end of the world is certainly worthy of a second glance.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.600
For surely, Patches isn't as straightforward as he seems

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.320
though you'd be forgiven for thinking otherwise.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.660
"There's a fine stash of treasure right down that hole..."

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.060
"I'll strip your corpse clean!"

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:50.200
"Wait now, you didn't actually fall down then; everybody makes mistakes."

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.760
"I'm not above it all, I swear. We're on the same side."

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.660
"I'm trusty Patches, the one and only!"

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:00.340
Patches is clearly in love with tricking everyone for profit

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.140
but for a man who allegedly reviles the greed of men

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.160
and claims to be devoid of all worldly wants

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.240
is the profit truly what drives him in this endless task?

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.620
I think his greed is a front

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.640
a facade designed to hide his true purpose

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.820
which is to punish the greed and the want of others.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.780
"Every age it seems is tainted by the greed of men"

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:32.220
"Rubbish to one such as I, devoid of all worldly wants."

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:35.660
Time and time again we're lured by our greed

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:42.000
eventually finding a somewhat loyal friend in Patches after our punishment is delivered.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:46.880
But across all these worlds there is one man that Patches truly befriends

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:51.820
and this friendship gives us a rare insight into what he values.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.940
This friendship is with Greirat.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:58.120
"Ah, I see you met Greirat. The slinking rodent."

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:00.980
"But he did me a good term back in Lothric Dungeon."

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.340
"Doubtless I should do something about that little debt."

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:06.340
"Well, maybe not."

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.300
"Well, I can hardly believe he's still standing." (laughs)

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:15.140
Greirat the thief once fancied himself a martyr for the poor

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.720
the Souls version of Robin Hood if you'd like.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.540
It was his concern for others that led him to climb the great wall to Lothric

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.040
where he freed Patches from the Lothric dungeon

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.900
before being locked away in a cell of his own awaiting your rescue.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.920
"I don't want to sit around and die a petty rat"

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.140
"and I consider myself your friend."

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.920
Indebted to you and with all those he loves dead

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.840
Greirat dedicates himself fully to your cause

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:47.760
even embarking upon suicidal thieving runs through the most dangerous territories.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:52.900
It's these actions that lead Patches to his uncharacteristic concern.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:56.620
"Hey, what happened to Greirat anyhow?"

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.500
"I haven't seen him at all lately."

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.900
"If you know where he's carried off to, be sure and tell me."

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:07.400
"Now I need to stock up, and if he's gone and croaked, he'll have left a gold mine"

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.680
(chuckles)

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.380
"What, gone all the way to Irithyll has he?"

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.740
"Huh, there can't be that much left of that frozen spool."

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:19.800
"The old rat, he's gone off the deep end this time."

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:23.700
He makes an effort to hide his affection for this man

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.280
though his actions betray that he cares.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.200
For -dressed once again in the armor of the onion knight to hide his identity

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:35.720
it's Patches, not Siegward, that actually rescues Greirat in Irithyll.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:40.340
"I might have died if it wasn't for that peculiar onion knight."

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.040
So of all the men to save, why Greirat?

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.820
Well Greirat is much like Patches you can see what they have in common.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:53.340
They're both petty thieves, yet Greirat is one who acts without concern for himself.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.420
He doesn't steal out of greed, so Patches respects him.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.080
"Off to Lothric? The castle of no return?"

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.520
"That ol' thief's lost it if he thinks he has a chance in there."

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:08.620
"It's not like he's new to this game. What's got into him?"

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.780
Yet Patches also does outlive him.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.520
The curse of life is the curse of want after all

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:19.860
and if we view greed as the reason that many hollow and die

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:24.780
then it makes sense that Patches is the one perfectly suited to resist the curse

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:30.100
by resisting want and greed entirely if he thrives upon punishing others for their greed.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:37.200
So with no want and grounded by his desire to punish others for their want and to trick them and trap them

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.740
Patches makes it to the end of the world.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.120
But slowly the world is ending

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:46.520
and soon there's no one left to lure into his traps.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:49.320
There's no one else to trick with their own greed.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:53.400
So it seems that Patches too, wavers in his duty

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:57.340
for here at world's end even he loses himself.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:02.800
Which gives us a glimpse of the good heart that he used to have before the world made him what he was.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.560
"I'm... a Hollow. Yes."

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:11.940
"I try to play it off, but I haven't a clue about my past."

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.100
"Who I was or what I lived for."

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:17.560
"Not even my own blessed name."

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.860
"You remember that treasure? Well"

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:26.180
"I fetched it for you. Here. Go ahead, it's yours."

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:30.060
"Maybe it'll help you with that solemn duty of yours."

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.420
"I'm off in search of the Purging Monument."

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:36.340
"Once I find it, everything will come back to me."

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.100
"Who I was; what I lived for."

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:43.700
"What my name was and what terrible grudges I held."

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:44.980
"I don't know."

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:48.820
"I just have this feeling that that's the kind of man I was."

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:52.620
The Purging Monument has the power to purge the undead curse

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.240
and restore one's humanity.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:59.860
Ironically, only by displaying humanity can it be found.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.280
"What did I come here in search of?"

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:05.920
"Damn. Stop it."

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:09.540
"I'm unbreakable. Unbreakable."

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.920
"Ah... Please."

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:17.240
"Someone tell me. Who am I?"

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.380
"Why am I here?"

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:22.780
With your help, Lapp can find the purging monument

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:25.180
and surely Lapp is to be trusted.

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:27.940
"Are you certain of that- no."

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:30.840
"Sorry I know you'd never lie to me."

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:33.320
"Thank you. Thank you kindly."

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:37.360
"I swear upon my birth name that I am your friend."

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:39.960
"No matter what might come out"

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.520
"no matter what I was, if you would do me the honor."

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:47.460
"Allow me to be a true friend. Always."

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:53.460
At first glance, what's to come simply seems like more of the same, from Lapp. From Patches.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:58.960
"Finally you've come. Now I know exactly who I was."

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:03.000
"And for that, I've a little thanks to be giving."

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:07.020
"Go this way and peep past the broken staircase."

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:10.980
"Some awfully fine treasures, just sitting there all alone."

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:13.080
"It'll change your life."

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:16.560
The swift kick down a hole fills you with frustration

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:20.340
till you realize that he's actually kicked you where you want to go.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:23.060
To the ledge that leads out of this graveyard.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.800
A setback that allows you to move forward.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:30.880
"Every age it seems is tainted by the greed of men."

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:37.280
"Rubbish to one such as I, devoid of all worldly wants."

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:42.420
(laughs)

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:50.260
"Hm.. I don't know. Maybe it's just the way we are."

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:53.580
"I'll stick you in my prayers."

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.160
"A fine dark soul to you."

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:02.220
For the first time, Patches helps you on your quest in a perfectly fitting way.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:05.160
He sets you on the path to the church of Filianore

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:10.400
where he assists you one last time in your quest to weaken the lord's grip on the Ringed City.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:14.620
He did always despise clerics, charlatans he calls them

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:21.060
and it's fitting beyond words that Patches would play a part in undoing the greatest lie of all.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:27.160
Undoing the greed of the gods that's rooted in faith, in Filianore, and in fire.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:30.900
Here, you both stand at the end of the world

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:35.380
undead, unbroken, yet we two could not be more different

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.020
Patches fought for no one but himself

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:41.340
for no cause other than to scoff at the greed of men.

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:48.260
But you, he's seen your kind time and time and time again, and he outlived you all.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:53.400
Those who lost everything and grasped for the faintest glimmer of hope.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:58.020
Kind-hearted fools doomed by the very light that guides them.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:04.140
He's seen men throw away their lives for the truth, for to an undead life is meaningless

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:11.460
Patches probably figures, why seek the truth when greater men have tried and gone mad as a result?

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:17.420
Even with the truth in tow, there is no fate for us other than the loss of self.

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:21.120
Because even if you're selfless, you can't save everyone.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:26.480
No... No matter how hard you tried, in the end you couldn't save a single soul

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:32.520
and the more you try to help, the more you fight against evil, the more you will lose.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:37.360
Before you're doomed to lose those closest to you. Family, friends.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.000
Some may even turn against you.

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.580
For even with your boundless compassion

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:46.840
no one can foretell the consequences of your good intentions.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:51.940
All of this, it's just want and greed in some shape or another.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:56.020
A desire to look back at something that made your life worthwhile.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.740
Whether it's a thirst for knowledge.

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.740
A desperate faith.

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:02.720
Some petty revenge.

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:08.020
It's taken some crestfallen men eons to find something worth fighting for

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:10.880
and even then they're fated to lose it all.

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:13.740
For even the gods are in despair.

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:16.080
The lords shy from their duty

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.780
and the last fire is fading.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:21.820
But something sets you two apart

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:25.100
and maybe the one thing that you both have in common

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:27.740
is that you never looked back?

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:32.840
Another thing I've never looked back from is switching from Skype to Discord

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:36.640
and you guys know that I've actually never done a sponsorship on this channel.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:42.880
But this is the exception because I've never been approached by a company that I believed in until now.

